cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "evacrl: tsunami evacuation guidance with reinforcement learning"
abstract: >-
  Agent-based simulation of a tsunami evacuation on a road network, with tabular reinforcement learning
  (Q-learning, SARSA, Monte Carlo) that guides evacuees at each intersection, a shortest-path baseline, a pipeline
  that builds a study area from OpenStreetMap, shelters and a census mesh, and an experiment layer (repeated runs,
  calibration, comparison, manifests).
type: software
version: 0.2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Mas
    given-names: Erick
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4861-5739"
repository-code: "https://github.com/erick2307/tsuevac"
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - tsunami
  - evacuation
  - reinforcement learning
  - agent-based simulation
  - disaster risk reduction
